<!-- 3. WHY IT WORKS: counter-position against one even pace -->
<section id="why" style="background:var(--cream)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rv" style="max-width:760px;margin-bottom:44px">
      <div class="kicker">Why it works</div>
      <h2>A pace calculator gives you one number. <em>That's how the wall finds you.</em></h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:16px">Divide 42.2 by your goal and you get one even pace from the gun. Your plan does 4 things a calculator can't.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fgrid">
      <div class="fcard rv">
        <div class="vs"><div><small>Even pace, 10K</small><strong>53:20</strong></div><div class="you"><small>Your plan, 10K</small><strong>54:00</strong></div></div>
        <h3>It starts you behind, on purpose</h3>
        <p>For a 3:45 you're about 40 seconds down at the 10K sign. They're the cheapest 40 seconds of your race, and they're what keeps you running at 32K.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fcard blue rv">
        <div class="big">1%</div>
        <h3>It builds in your watch's error</h3>
        <p>A GPS watch reads about 1% long in a race. Your paces are a few seconds quick to cover it, so the chip still says your goal when your watch says 42.6.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fcard rv">
        <div class="big">30g</div>
        <h3>It puts your fuel on the clock</h3>
        <p>First gel at 20 minutes, then every 30, with water. That's 60g of carbs an hour, timed to the minute, plus how many to carry.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fcard rv">
        <div class="big">2:00</div>
        <h3>It leaves room for a portaloo</h3>
        <p>Every plan finishes a couple of minutes under your goal. Stop for a portaloo and you go straight back to your pace. No panic sprint.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="center rv" style="margin-top:40px"><a class="btn" href="#get-plan">Get my plan <span class="arr">→</span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>

